# Mapping rules are code

Canonical statement: `CLAUDE.md`. Read it before changing how any venue
market maps.

- Leagues, market types, selection vocab, venue league ids and aliases
  live in Python under `mappers/` (table of locations in `CLAUDE.md`).
- A mapping change is a code edit plus a test next to it, then
  `GCP_PROJECT=rs-marketmaking .venv/bin/pytest -q`, then an MR. The
  `regression:mapping-gate` CI job (`regression/live_gate.py`) shows the
  row delta. Removed rows need a waiver in `regression/waivers.toml`.
- The BigQuery rule-set tip (`mappers/seed/sot.py`, `mapping_*` tables,
  `P_*` / `S0_*` rule sets) is legacy. Parts of the mapper still load it.
  Do not add leagues, rules, aliases or pins to it, and do not make new
  code read it.
- The mapping console, `mappers/control_plane/` and Mapper Chat are not a
  way to ship mapping. Do not stage pins, approve cards or extend them.
- No ticker, slug or symbol parsing. Sides and identity come from typed
  venue fields.
- Unit tests read a frozen tip from `tests/fixtures/sot/tip.json`
  (`MAPPING_SOT_FIXTURE`, set in `tests/conftest.py`). Do not edit that
  fixture to make a mapping change pass.
